# The built artifacts. DELIBERATELY NOT TRACKED: a release has a distribution
# channel of its own — the release page — so a tracked copy here would be a
# second, silently drifting one, at about 7 MB per build in history that nothing
# reads. The same reasoning retired the far-end bundle (farend/.gitignore), and
# what a build is measured against is now a record rather than a binary: the
# "testedBuild" block of docs/support-matrix.md.
#
# What IS tracked in release/ is everything a rebuild needs: the installer, the
# uninstaller, the in-archive README, the release-page text, the build script
# and the install/uninstall test. `make-release.sh` reproduces dist/ from them.
dist/
